<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.50%" pitch="-2.50%">
            Certain Chaldeans came forward and reported Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego to the king.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            These men, they said, pay no attention to you.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            They do not serve your gods.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            They do not worship the golden image you have set up.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            The king's fury was great.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            He had Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego brought before him.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            And he gave them one last chance.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            He would play the music again.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            They could still bow.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            They could still be saved.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            But — he said, and the threat was plain —
            <break time="500ms"/>
            who is the god that will deliver you out of my hands?
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Their answer was unhurried.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            "O Nebuchadnezzar, we have no need to answer you in this matter.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Our God whom we serve is able to deliver us
            <break time="500ms"/>
            from the burning fiery furnace.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            He will deliver us out of your hand, O king.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            But if not —
            <break time="500ms"/>
            be it known to you, O king,
            <break time="500ms"/>
            that we will not serve your gods
            <break time="500ms"/>
            or worship the golden image that you have set up."
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            But if not.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            Three words that hold the full weight of real faith.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            Not certainty of the outcome.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Certainty of the God.
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
